# Environment variables and secrets
.env
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# API keys and credentials
*api_key*
*credentials*
*secret*
!.secrets.baseline
# Source module, NOT a secret — the broad *secret* glob above would otherwise
# drop it from the repo (it did: PR #77 merged without it → CI ModuleNotFoundError).
!src/security/secret_box.py
# ...and its TEST file, for the identical reason. The *secret* glob caught this one too, and it went
# unnoticed for ~7 weeks: tests/test_secret_box.py existed locally from 2026-06-19 but was never
# committed, so CI never ran a single one of its 13 tests while src/security/secret_box.py — tracked,
# shipped, security-relevant code — sat at 68% coverage. It surfaced only because a local test count
# (3200) disagreed with a fresh clone (3187). Rescuing the module without its test is half a fix.
!tests/test_secret_box.py
